# Line endings, pinned so a clone cannot break the tools.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` (this machine's setting) keeps the working tree CRLF and the repository LF.
# That is invisible until someone clones with `autocrlf=false` or `input` — and then every `.cmd`
# arrives as LF, which breaks `%~dp0` handling in `tools\run.cmd` and `tools\apply-host-patch.cmd`.
# The repo has a test that .cmd files are CRLF in the WORKING TREE, so that clone would ship a
# package whose own test suite cannot run. Pin it here instead of relying on a client setting.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Everything else normalises to LF in the repository.
*.js   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
